# HDFC Banking AI — Architecture Diagrams

This file contains the logical system architecture, RAG preparation/retrieval flow, and deployment topology.

## 1. Logical system architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    U[Customer / Administrator] --> FE[Web Frontend<br/>HTML, CSS, JavaScript]
    FE <-->|HTTPS / JSON| API[FastAPI Backend]
    API --> AUTH[Authentication & Session Services]
    API --> ROUTER[Intent Router]
    API --> PROFILE[Profile & Transaction APIs]
    API --> ADMIN[Admin APIs]
    AUTH --> DB[(Neon PostgreSQL<br/>Customer data + RAG data)]
    PROFILE --> DB
    ADMIN --> DB
    ROUTER -->|LLM_ONLY / RAG / SQL / SQL_RAG| CHAT[Chat Orchestration Service]
    CHAT -->|Predict intent| MODEL[Fine-tuned Qwen Model API]
    CHAT -->|Generate answer| MODEL
    CHAT -->|Authenticated customer SQL| DB
    CHAT -->|Knowledge question| RAG[RAG Retrieval Pipeline]
    RAG --> INGEST[Document Ingestion<br/>Audit • Clean • Chunk • Embed]
    INGEST -->|Store document chunks and embeddings| DB
    RAG --> SEARCH[Hybrid Retrieval<br/>BM25 + pgvector similarity search]
    DB -->|RAG chunks, metadata and vectors| SEARCH
    SEARCH -->|Retrieved passages + source metadata| CHAT
    CHAT -->|Grounded / fallback / abstention response| API
    API --> FE
```

## 2. RAG knowledge preparation and retrieval

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[Source Workbook / Documents] --> B[Audit]
    B --> C[Clean & Deduplicate]
    C --> D[Canonical Documents]
    D --> E[Chunking]
    E --> F[Embedding Generation]
    F --> G[(Neon PostgreSQL<br/>pgvector + RAG chunks)]
    G --> H[Vector Similarity Retrieval]
    G --> I[Keyword Retrieval]
    H --> J[RRF Hybrid Ranking]
    I --> J
    J --> K[Evidence / Abstention Decision]
    K --> L[Grounded Answer Generation]
```

## 3. Deployment architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    USER[Evaluator / User Browser]
    FE[Render: Frontend<br/>HDFC Banking AI]
    BE[Render: FastAPI Backend<br/>HDFC Banking AI Backend]
    DB[(Neon PostgreSQL<br/>Customer data + RAG vectors)]
    NG[ngrok HTTPS Tunnel]
    COLAB[Google Colab GPU<br/>Fine-tuned Qwen Inference API]
    USER -->|HTTPS| FE
    FE -->|API requests| BE
    BE --> DB
    BE -->|MODEL_API_URL + bearer token| NG
    NG --> COLAB
```

## Architecture rationale

- The frontend, backend, model inference, retrieval, and structured-data access have separate responsibilities.
- Neon PostgreSQL is the single database for customer records and RAG document chunks, embeddings, and related metadata.
- The backend handles authentication, routing, orchestration, and customer-specific database access.
- The language model is used for intent prediction and answer generation; it is not the authorization layer for customer records.
- Hybrid retrieval combines semantic vector retrieval with keyword retrieval, then uses Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF) to combine rankings.
- The model inference service runs separately from the Render web services, allowing GPU-based inference without loading the model into the web backend host.

## Deployment note

The deployed frontend and backend are separate Render services. The backend calls the model inference API through the configured `MODEL_API_URL` and `MODEL_API_TOKEN`. In the current demonstration setup, the inference API runs in Google Colab and is exposed through ngrok. The model service therefore depends on the Colab runtime and tunnel remaining available.
